<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 17:12:50 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Europe</category><title>France, Germany seek new EU rapid response tool against trade threats</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261005-france-germany-seek-new-eu-rapid-response-tool-against-trade-threats</link><description>
France and Germany proposed a new legal tool to enable the EU to respond rapidly to trade wars or measures, such as dumping, that could economically harm the bloc. While French President Emmanuel Macron and German Chancellor Friedrich Merz said the proposal was not a direct response to the actions of any particular country, it came days before EU Chief Ursula von der Leyen visits China to tackle trade fictions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/69ed86b4-c0d7-11f1-ab18-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2G89HV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/69ed86b4-c0d7-11f1-ab18-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2G89HV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1a65e7e8-c0d8-11f1-a6d7-7fb3625627f4</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 17:01:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/69ed86b4-c0d7-11f1-ab18-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2G89HV.jpg">© Ina Fassbender, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>ICC unseals arrest warrants for Taliban education ministers</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261005-icc-unseals-arrest-warrants-for-taliban-education-ministers</link><description></description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29e5acbc-c0d8-11f1-b47f-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/3db6bdc9c05a26eff7530fb3aa39d6136044aeb4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29e5acbc-c0d8-11f1-b47f-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/3db6bdc9c05a26eff7530fb3aa39d6136044aeb4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2a9e99b6-c0d8-11f1-9fa9-714e37cd4f2b</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 16:16:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29e5acbc-c0d8-11f1-b47f-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/3db6bdc9c05a26eff7530fb3aa39d6136044aeb4.jpg">© Wakil KOHSAR / AFP/File</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French high school students predict escalation of protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-french-high-school-students-predict-escalation-of-protests</link><description>
Lessons were suspended at hundreds of French high schools on Monday, as part of a wave of student protests over learning conditions that have rocked the European nation. Larger demonstrations are expected on Tuesday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b70c2724-c0d3-11f1-9cd6-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/france-8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b70c2724-c0d3-11f1-9cd6-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/france-8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d366a214-c0d3-11f1-83ca-75b8bce16c9b</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 15:57:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>ISIS suspects face 'outsourced' justice in Iraq as HRW warns of 'collective global detention crisis'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-isis-suspects-face-outsourced-justice-in-iraq-as-hrw-warns-of-collective-global-detention-crisis-1</link><description>
Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Letta Tayler, Senior Counterterrorism Advisor at Human Rights Watch. She warns of the detention of suspected Islamic State members transferred from northeast Syria to Iraq as part of a much wider "global detention crisis". The men and boys now held in Iraq are living in 'dire' conditions, including deaths from illness, allegations of torture, and serious questions surrounding access to effective legal representation. Can accountability be achieved through legal proceedings that respect the rule of law and provide genuine justice to both detainees and victims?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1f0c0f28-c0cb-11f1-abfc-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-151326-152657-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1f0c0f28-c0cb-11f1-abfc-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-151326-152657-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2424c5e0-c0cb-11f1-834e-a9d28765d43a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 15:46:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>How Lula’s successes in Brazil may have paved the way for his presidential defeat</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-how-lulas-successes-in-brazil-may-have-paved-the-way-for-his-presidential-defeat</link><description>
Brazil’s veteran leftist President Luiz Inacio "Lula" da Silva trailed Flavio Bolsonaro, the son of his far-right predecessor, in the first-round presidential vote on Sunday. Some analysts suggest that the sweeping anti-poverty measures Lula put in place over two decades may have helped give rise to a growing lower-middle class drawn to the far right’s promise to get the government out of people’s lives.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b44c1f6a-c0c1-11f1-8f3f-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-05T051605Z-1725054154-RC2OWNAEUWVT-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-ELECTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b44c1f6a-c0c1-11f1-8f3f-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-05T051605Z-1725054154-RC2OWNAEUWVT-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-ELECTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">21e5e520-c0c1-11f1-88e0-851ca5bd765a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 15:21:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b44c1f6a-c0c1-11f1-8f3f-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-05T051605Z-1725054154-RC2OWNAEUWVT-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-ELECTION.jpg">© Brian Snyder, Reuters</source><dc:creator>Paul MILLAR</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>7.4 million visitors, 6.7 million litres of beer: Oktoberfest comes to an end</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-7-4-million-visitors-6-7-million-litres-of-beer-oktoberfest-comes-to-an-end</link><description>
Germany's famous celebration of autumn and beer, Oktoberfest, wrapped up this weekend withthis year saw record attendence with 7.4 million visitors descending on the festival. The majority of attendees came from within Germany, with Americans, Italians and Austrians topping the numbers for foreign visitors
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6ced5c9a-c0cd-11f1-8805-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-153925-154106-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6ced5c9a-c0cd-11f1-8805-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-153925-154106-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">724e8e48-c0cd-11f1-8c0c-03f62142e242</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 15:04:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French school protests continue with larger demonstrations set for Tuesday</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-french-school-protests-continue-with-larger-demonstrations-set-for-tuesday</link><description>
Lessons were suspended at hundreds of French high schools on Monday, as part of a wave of student protest over learning conditions that have rocked the country. An even larger day of demonstrations is expected on Tuesday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a85a51ee-c0cc-11f1-b2c2-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-152732-152936-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a85a51ee-c0cc-11f1-b2c2-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-152732-152936-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aceef0b6-c0cc-11f1-8c0f-6318e0ab2632</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 15:03:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'I could feel the petrol dripping': The violent attacks that have marred France school protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-i-could-feel-the-petrol-dripping-the-violent-attacks-that-have-marred-france-school-protests</link><description><![CDATA[
Between 400-500 schools across France are expected to stay closed this Monday, as student protests continue. Pupils are calling for smaller class sizes and better equipped classrooms. More than 70 schoolteachers have been injured since the unrest began. Ellen Gainsford & France 2 take a look at some of the violent incidents related to the protests.
]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e2763d9e-c0cb-11f1-bf77-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-143209-143415-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e2763d9e-c0cb-11f1-bf77-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-143209-143415-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e810ce68-c0cb-11f1-a5e4-592b80040dc5</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 15:01:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Yemen government forces announce offensive on Houthi-held territory</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-yemen-government-forces-announce-offensive-on-houthi-held-territory</link><description>
The internationally recognised Yemeni government announced on Sunday the launch of an offensive ‌to recapture territory held by Houthi rebels, with President Rashad al-Alimi swearing to fight "until the country is liberated from the grip of the terrorist militia".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/07abbf54-c0cb-11f1-949b-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-141904-142040-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/07abbf54-c0cb-11f1-949b-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-141904-142040-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0c629ab8-c0cb-11f1-ba24-b1fcc3233890</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 14:59:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump names head of new 'Super Intelligence Force' to oversee AI</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-trump-names-head-of-new-super-intelligence-force-to-oversee-ai</link><description>
US President Donald Trump said on Sunday he had named Director of National Intelligence ​Jay Clayton the ‌administration's AI czar, tasking him with coordinating the federal government's efforts to maintain ⁠US leadership in the technology. Trump, who has pushed to rename artificial intelligence as "super intelligence," said Clayton would head the newly created Super Intelligence Force (SIF).
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e71762e-c0cc-11f1-8611-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-144258-144434-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e71762e-c0cc-11f1-8611-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-144258-144434-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">230b266c-c0cc-11f1-a654-6318e0ab2632</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 14:59:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Down to Earth</category><title>Frenchwoman buys elephants from abusive owners in Laos</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20261005-frenchwoman-buys-elephants-from-abusive-owners-in-laos</link><description>
Once known as "The Land of a Million Elephants", only an estimated 800 elephants remain in Laos, as deforestation and exploitation push the species closer than ever to the brink of extinction. Despite the dwindling numbers, a Frenchwoman has made it her mission to give ageing elephants a new home, buying them from their abusive owners. Our France 2 colleagues report, with FRANCE 24's Andrew Hilliar.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f9370a6e-be63-11f1-8447-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/Capture-d-e%CC%81cran-2026-10-01-a%CC%80-12-08-42.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f9370a6e-be63-11f1-8447-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/Capture-d-e%CC%81cran-2026-10-01-a%CC%80-12-08-42.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">84e11cd0-c0c1-11f1-9eb7-bf316aba2c5a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 14:44:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Andrew HILLIAR</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>Sulaf and Late Again on uprooting and reconnecting with their heritage</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261005-sulaf-and-late-again-on-uprooting-and-reconnecting-with-their-heritage</link><description>
This week, Marjorie Hache has the pleasure of sitting down with Sudan's Sulaf, who is releasing her debut album "Aba", a poetic exploration of traditional Sudanese music with a contemporary twist and which she recorded in Paris where she has been living in exile since 2022.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61fc6758-c0ba-11f1-8d16-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/CULTURE-05-10-2026-11-14-ING34-CLEAN-B-frame-43837.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61fc6758-c0ba-11f1-8d16-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/CULTURE-05-10-2026-11-14-ING34-CLEAN-B-frame-43837.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e69590bc-c0b9-11f1-8b73-8b8fd21a75e1</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 14:29:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marjorie HACHE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Macron slams Russia’s ‘irresponsible’ strikes on Ukraine’s civilian infrastructure</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261005-macron-slams-russia-s-irresponsible-strikes-on-ukraine-s-civilian-infrastructure</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron on Monday slammed Russia's increased strikes on Ukrainian civilian infrastructure. In a phone call with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, Macron said he reviewed "the concrete support" Europe can provide Ukraine to defend itself against the attacks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/04870d1a-b838-11f1-8deb-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8PA9J8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/04870d1a-b838-11f1-8deb-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8PA9J8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ec399618-c0c2-11f1-a0e0-5dc43ddc7b2d</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 14:09:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/04870d1a-b838-11f1-8deb-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8PA9J8.jpg">© Thomas Samson, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Spain: 'Mini-hurricane' kills at least two people in Catalonia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-spain-mini-hurricane-kills-at-least-two-people-in-catalonia</link><description>
Two people have ⁠died and ​another is missing after heavy rains and flooding in Spain's ​Catalonia region, authorities said on Sunday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d1657306-c0c3-11f1-aa1e-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/spain-11.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d1657306-c0c3-11f1-aa1e-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/spain-11.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0b3617ac-c0c4-11f1-b92e-cdd0df4b4078</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 13:58:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump heads to Nebraska as Republicans fear strongholds could flip</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-trump-heads-to-nebraska-as-republicans-fear-strongholds-could-flip</link><description>
US President ​Donald Trump will visit Nebraska on Monday to rally Republicans and promote his economic ​record, taking his message of new investment and manufacturing to a state where farmers and truckers face sharply higher diesel prices and voters worry about inflation. His stop in ​the ‌city of Grand Island is part of Trump's 32-day ⁠sprint to the November 3 midterm elections, a campaign in which he is spending considerable time in ‌Republican strongholds. Trump has urged Republicans to “pretend” he is on the ballot, ⁠arguing that voters should view the midterms as a referendum on his administration and economic record. France 24's Fraser Jackson has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d232afe4-c0bc-11f1-b2a9-578a4b968fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-141248-141746-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d232afe4-c0bc-11f1-b2a9-578a4b968fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-141248-141746-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d736c2e6-c0bc-11f1-a512-894e3aeff6e4</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 13:05:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France high school protests: Can the government regain control?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-france-high-school-protests-can-the-government-regain-control</link><description>
Up to 500 schools are expected to be totally or partially closed in France as student protests continue to rock the country. The demonstrations, which have been going on for over two weeks, have spread nationwide and are set to continue and the unrest appears to have caught the Macron government off guard. The protests have confronted French security forces with a daunting task, and the situation is likely to feature at this week's cabinet meeting, where the interior and justice minister will warn that there are few police resources to deploy.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5953ae0e-c0ba-11f1-bf12-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-133212-133343-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5953ae0e-c0ba-11f1-bf12-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-133212-133343-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5f2193c8-c0ba-11f1-8151-b915cdfca0ef</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 13:03:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Japan bids farewell to Asian Games after fortnight of turmoil and records</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-japan-bids-farewell-to-asian-games-after-fortnight-of-turmoil-and-records</link><description>
The 20th Asian Games closed on Sunday after a rocky fortnight lit ​up by youthful brilliance in the sporting arenas but tempered by logistical dysfunction and subdued public interest. Olympic Council of Asia (OCA) President Sheikh Joaan bin Hamad Al Thani declared the Games closed at Mizuho Park Athletic Stadium, with the torch handed to organisers of the next event in Doha 2030.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d85df962-c0b9-11f1-9c24-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-131859-132039-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d85df962-c0b9-11f1-9c24-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-131859-132039-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dd3171da-c0b9-11f1-97e3-db49ece6c591</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 13:01:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US bombers leave UK air base amid 'new threats': What we know so far</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-us-bombers-leave-uk-air-base-amid-new-threats-what-we-know-so-far</link><description>
The United States confirmed that it had withdrawn all B-1 bombers from the British airbase of RAF Fairford, reportedly due to "new threats," with Britain's government insisting Monday the site is safe. France 24's Philip Turle takes a look at what we know so far.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b7573422-c0b9-11f1-a7bb-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-131453-131805-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b7573422-c0b9-11f1-a7bb-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-131453-131805-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bc55a314-c0b9-11f1-8ee8-db49ece6c591</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 13:00:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ethiopian govt retakes Tigray capital as rebels pull out</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-ethiopian-govt-retakes-tigray-capital-as-rebels-pull-out</link><description>
Pro-government forces have regained control of the capital of Tigray, they said on Sunday, dealing a major setback to the opposition alliance that rules the ​northern Ethiopian region.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e64bd20-c0af-11f1-ad15-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-111136-111303-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e64bd20-c0af-11f1-ad15-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-111136-111303-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">234b205e-c0af-11f1-8e74-8b5ca5b06054</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 12:57:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Very bad result for Lula: Bolsonaro is far more effective at speaking to that growing middle class'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/very-bad-result-for-lula-bolsonaro-is-far-more-effective-at-speaking-to-that-growing-middle-class</link><description>
Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome Felipe Krause, the head of Oxford University's Brazilian Studies Programme. Brazil's election reflects a political landscape that has become increasingly polarized, explains Krause. And he describes the current mood as one of “tired polarization: People are just exhausted. They feel that the political class is just kind of offering more of the same". The first round reveals a significant consolidation of the Brazilian right in government. Brazil's expanding middle class is increasingly attracted to entrepreneurialism and individualism, constituencies that "Bolsonarismo" has proved particularly effective at reaching.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02676028-c091-11f1-a552-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-080339-081250-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02676028-c091-11f1-a552-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-080339-081250-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">07b1760e-c091-11f1-981a-6b7cf4bcc737</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 12:54:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>Brazil presidential election: 'Bolsonaro being ahead is a surprise,' researcher says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261005-brazil-presidential-election-bolsonaro-being-ahead-is-a-surprise-researcher-says</link><description>
Far-right candidate Flavio Bolsonaro has pulled off a surprise win in the first round of Brazil’s presidential election. He defied most polls to win with 47 percent, compared to 45 percent for leftist incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula de Silva. We spoke to Thomas Zicman de Barros, a research fellow at CEVIPOF, the political research centre at Sciences Po University, and columnist for our sister radio station RFI. He told us that never before in Brazilian history has a candidate who was behind in the first round then succeeded in the second.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1adb6bc6-c0ba-11f1-8052-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15118627956ac39b00d5d4f1-95598905.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1adb6bc6-c0ba-11f1-8052-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15118627956ac39b00d5d4f1-95598905.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">12dd0672-c098-11f1-a16a-97a620563070</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 12:52:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Stuart NORVAL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Mountaineer takes cancer research and quality of life to new heights... 8,000 metres, to be precise!</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/mountaineer-takes-cancer-research-and-quality-of-life-to-new-heights-8-000-metres-to-be-precise</link><description>
Delano D’Souza is pleased to welcome Dr Shauna Burke, Associate Professor in Exercise and Health Psychology at the University of Leeds. A passionate mountaineer who first summited Mount Everest in 2005, Dr Burke returned to the world’s highest mountain earlier this year, following her diagnosis with stage four breast cancer. She is now setting her sights on the world's 13 other 8,000-metre peaks. For Dr Burke, the mountains are more than a backdrop to an extraordinary personal challenge. “When I’m in the mountains, I do feel at peace. I feel alive,” she says. Faced with an incurable cancer diagnosis, she chose not to allow the illness to define the boundaries of her life. she , continuing to explore what exercise, resilience and a commitment to living fully might make possible. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4c607792-c0b8-11f1-94ce-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8844352436ac397f904b896-37965471.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4c607792-c0b8-11f1-94ce-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8844352436ac397f904b896-37965471.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1af45706-c0a8-11f1-ad81-b3aee1e3727f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 11:16:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Indian police detain demonstrators as protests over voter roll revision intensify</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-ndian-police-detain-demonstrators-as-protests-over-voter-roll-revision-intensify</link><description>
